<svg viewBox="-2 -14 222 120" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1">
  {/* The whole vehicle carries three degrees of bow-down trim: level, it
      was parked. The ring stays outside the trim so it scales true. */}
  <g transform="rotate(3 106 60)">
    {/* Tether off a padeye aft of centre, trailing up and AFT: the vehicle
        flies away from its cage and the umbilical follows it down. The eye
        is kept low; a tall bail on a flat top was a knob on a lid. */}
    <path d="M81 8C78 2 70-5 56-14" stroke-width="0.6" opacity="0.5" />
    <path d="M77 12V9.5A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 78.5 8h5A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 85 9.5V12" stroke-width="0.8" />
    {/* Syntactic foam: one solid slab, the heaviest line on the vehicle
        and the only closed shape, overhanging the frame a little at each
        end and bevelled under the nose the way Hercules and Jason are cut
        back to give the cameras their view. The top corners are chamfered
        the way machined foam is; sharp, the slab was a brick. Nothing
        drawn inside it, so it reads as solid against the cage. */}
    <path d="M30 12h130l4 4v14l-8 10H26V16z" />
    {/* Near posts and rail, each member run past its joint the way welded
        tube meets, and the outer posts run up into the foam so slab and
        cage are one body: corners that close are a briefcase. The far
        posts are ghosted up and aft of the near ones, because seeing the
        other side through the bays is what makes an open frame read open
        at true size; a far rail as well closed it into a tray. One
        diagonal, in the aft bay only, says truss; one in every bay said
        window. The foam's underside is the top rail. */}
    <path d="M30 37v61M76 40v58M156 37v61" stroke-width="0.9" />
    <path d="M26 94h134" stroke-width="0.9" />
    <path d="M25 40v49M71 40v49M151 40v49" stroke-width="0.5" opacity="0.4" />
    <path d="M30 94 76 40" stroke-width="0.5" opacity="0.45" />
    {/* Aft thruster, vectored, mounted at the frame corner where an HD
        carries it: a duct seen a quarter on, the near rim an ellipse, the
        shroud running in across the post to a narrower far rim inside the
        bay, and the hub with its shaft the only thing inside. Blades made
        it a fan icon; a disc on edge made it a ring with marks. */}
    <ellipse cx="20" cy="64" rx="7" ry="14" stroke-width="0.9" />
    <path d="M20 50 30 52.5M20 78 30 75.5" stroke-width="0.7" />
    <ellipse cx="30" cy="64" rx="4.5" ry="11.5" stroke-width="0.5" opacity="0.6" />
    <circle cx="24" cy="64" r="2" stroke-width="0.7" />
    <path d="M26 64h5" stroke-width="0.5" opacity="0.7" />
    {/* One pressure housing inside, a tube with an end-cap rule at each
        end, run across the mid post because kit in a real frame does not
        stop at the members. Everything else that was drawn in the frame
        went, so the rest of it shows through. */}
    <path d="M64 60h72v12H64zM68 60v12M132 60v12" stroke-width="0.55" opacity="0.5" />
    {/* Forward: one pan-and-tilt column hung from the bevel to the frame,
        carrying both lamps and the camera, so the front is one fitting
        rather than three floating on stubs. Both lamp faces are lit, and
        between them they throw one cone, forward and down, which is where
        an ROV looks; a beam pointing up was an antenna. The camera and
        the jaw sit inside the cone, because the cone is what they are
        for. */}
    <path d="M159 36v28M156 48h3M156 62h3" stroke-width="0.7" />
    <path d="M160 33h9a3 3 0 0 1 0 6h-9z" stroke-width="0.7" transform="rotate(4 160 36)" />
    <path d="M160 44.5h10a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7h-10z" stroke-width="0.7" transform="rotate(18 160 48)" />
    <path d="M169 37 208 40M170 51 206 74" stroke-width="0.5" stroke-dasharray="3 4" opacity="0.5" />
    <path d="M162 58h12v8h-12zM174 57v10" stroke-width="0.75" />
    <circle cx="162" cy="62" r="1.6" stroke-width="0.6" />
    <circle cx="169" cy="36.6" r="1.8" fill="currentColor" class="drift__telemetry" />
    <circle cx="169.5" cy="51.1" r="2" fill="currentColor" class="drift__telemetry" />
    {/* Manipulator off the forward post, elbow up, forearm reaching
        forward and down into the light. Hung from the bottom corner with
        the elbow down it was a folding table leg. The links are bars, two
        lines each, because a single stroke ending in a V was an antenna.
        Straight links; a curve here reads as a hose. */}
    <circle cx="158" cy="80" r="3" stroke-width="0.8" />
    <path d="M158.9 81.4 180.9 67.4M157.1 78.7 179.1 64.7" stroke-width="0.8" />
    <circle cx="180" cy="66" r="2.6" stroke-width="0.7" />
    <path d="M179.3 67.2 203.3 81.2M180.7 64.8 204.7 78.8" stroke-width="0.8" />
    <circle cx="204" cy="80" r="1.8" stroke-width="0.7" />
    <path d="m204 80 8-4 2 2M204 80l7 4 2-2" stroke-width="0.7" />
    {/* Two skid runners, fore and aft, unequal, the forward toe turned
        up, and nothing under the middle: one runner the full width closed
        the frame into a plinth. */}
    <path d="M40 94v6M60 94v6M104 94v6M144 94v6" stroke-width="0.7" />
    <path d="M32 100h34M98 100h50l8-5" stroke-width="0.8" />
  </g>
  <circle cx="106" cy="58" r="44" class="drift__ring" />
</svg>
<span class="drift__tag">ROV-01 &middot; Fl(2) 5s</span>
